WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.008
[opening theme music playing]

01:04.147 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:06.066 --> 01:07.358
[man 1] Whoa!

01:07.442 --> 01:09.360
[man 2] Careful. Careful.

01:09.444 --> 01:11.112
-One, two.
-[grunting]

01:11.196 --> 01:12.572
[middle-aged Ae-sun] Wait. Lift it higher.

01:12.655 --> 01:15.408
[Geum-myeong] The road ahead
could be a million miles long…

01:15.492 --> 01:18.536
Oh! No, I told you to be careful!

01:18.620 --> 01:21.331
If this breaks, I'm going to kill myself.
Be gentle.

01:21.414 --> 01:23.833
[Geum-myeong] But the greatest worry
you will ever have

01:23.917 --> 01:25.460
is the one in front of you.

01:25.543 --> 01:27.295
[man 2] Sir? Can you help lift?

01:27.378 --> 01:28.630
One, two, three.

01:29.339 --> 01:32.050
Hey, Mom?
Did we really have to bring that thing?

01:32.133 --> 01:34.511
It's huge! There's nowhere to put it.

01:35.470 --> 01:37.597
Where is this supposed to fit
in that tiny apartment?

01:37.680 --> 01:40.892
[sighs, groans] This was my dowry.

01:41.392 --> 01:43.019
The first nice thing I ever had.

01:43.103 --> 01:46.523
If you're really downsizing,
you shouldn't have brought so much stuff.

01:46.606 --> 01:50.443
Who on earth brings a mother-of-pearl
wardrobe when they move? Seriously.

01:50.527 --> 01:51.986
That's Tongyeong mother-of-pearl.

01:52.070 --> 01:52.904
Huh?

01:52.987 --> 01:55.406
[man 2] All right. Let's go. Let's go.
Let's take it up.

01:55.490 --> 01:56.324
-Okay. Come on.
-Okay.

01:56.407 --> 01:58.201
-Let's do it.
-Take that side.

01:58.284 --> 01:59.244
-Okay.
-Tip it over.

01:59.327 --> 02:00.537
-One, two.
-Wait.

02:00.620 --> 02:01.704
[grunting]

02:01.788 --> 02:02.789
God.

02:02.872 --> 02:05.166
-[man 2] Turn it this way.
-Why did we have to move away?

02:05.250 --> 02:08.753
-That brat gets whatever she wants.
-Who are you calling a brat, huh?

02:08.837 --> 02:12.257
You know Cheol-yong's sister actually
gives him some of her pay as an usher.

02:13.925 --> 02:14.926
What about her?

02:15.009 --> 02:16.803
Is she leading this family
or tearing it apart?

02:17.387 --> 02:18.513
You…

02:20.515 --> 02:22.600
You're always giving me a hard time, Dad.

02:23.101 --> 02:24.727
What have you done to your hair?

02:24.811 --> 02:27.147
Are you trying to make
the other kids at school laugh?

02:27.856 --> 02:31.025
-[man 1] Pull on your end.
-[man 2] Okay, get ready. Lift! Lift!

02:31.651 --> 02:33.194
[grunting]

02:34.779 --> 02:36.114
[sighs]

02:39.993 --> 02:41.452
[middle-aged Ae-sun sighs]

02:48.459 --> 02:49.752
Why won't this…

02:53.506 --> 02:54.591
Oh my God.

02:59.846 --> 03:02.432
So what's it for? Our dirty shoes?

03:02.515 --> 03:03.850
[middle-aged Ae-sun sighs]

03:06.436 --> 03:07.562
[moans]

03:08.521 --> 03:10.440
[Eun-myeong] Why aren't the aunties here?

03:11.357 --> 03:14.569
They couldn't wait to come by
for my circumcision. Where are they now?

03:14.652 --> 03:17.238
[middle-aged Ae-sun] The aunties are busy
because of the Olympics.

03:19.032 --> 03:20.116
Wait, I don't get it.

03:21.326 --> 03:23.077
I thought they hated the Olympics.

03:23.161 --> 03:25.371
-They're Jeju's representatives.
-Ah!

03:25.455 --> 03:27.916
The government decided
to give the haenyeo a role,

03:28.499 --> 03:30.168
so the aunties made amends.

03:30.668 --> 03:32.837
[Eun-myeong] Well,
isn't that convenient for them.

03:35.840 --> 03:38.593
Where do you think you're going?
You promised me you'd study.

03:38.676 --> 03:41.221
[grunts] So I can go to
a pricey school too?

03:41.888 --> 03:44.307
Then what? Are you gonna move into a hut?

03:45.350 --> 03:49.312
What happens to your precious dowry, then?
Your mother-of-pearl wardrobe?

03:50.188 --> 03:52.649
Oh my God.
I feed you well enough, don't I?

03:52.732 --> 03:55.693
Why is it always about money?
Is that all that you--

03:55.777 --> 03:56.819
Don't waste power.

03:57.612 --> 03:59.447
Are you going to Cheol-yong's again?

04:25.473 --> 04:27.475
[wistful music playing]

04:30.937 --> 04:32.146
[sighs]

04:37.193 --> 04:38.361
[sighs]

04:42.407 --> 04:43.449
[door opens]

04:46.035 --> 04:47.662
[music fades]

04:47.745 --> 04:48.579
Come here.

05:03.094 --> 05:05.847
[middle-aged Ae-sun]
You know what? This is better.

05:05.930 --> 05:07.140
A little better.

05:07.640 --> 05:10.935
I'll do the living room next.
All with your favorite flower.

05:11.519 --> 05:13.104
Oh, it's already peeling.

05:15.189 --> 05:17.191
You chose a good place for the wardrobe.

05:17.942 --> 05:20.069
When you get home,
you can hang your clothes right away.

05:20.153 --> 05:21.321
It works perfectly.

05:21.404 --> 05:23.489
You're just a bit smarter
with these kinds of things.

05:23.573 --> 05:24.866
You make good choices.

05:24.949 --> 05:27.076
Why are you so talkative all of a sudden?

05:28.995 --> 05:31.122
You think florals would work
for the curtains?

05:31.748 --> 05:34.042
Let's do it. I have the store's number.

05:34.751 --> 05:36.669
-I'll… I'll call--
-It's all right.

05:39.088 --> 05:40.715
I like this place already.

05:43.426 --> 05:44.385
[sighs]

05:45.720 --> 05:48.222
It was just bringing up the wardrobe.

05:48.806 --> 05:50.892
You know how important it is to me.

05:51.642 --> 05:53.478
That's why I lost my temper earlier.

05:54.103 --> 05:55.521
[laughs]

05:55.605 --> 05:58.066
[groans] Now she laughs?

05:59.359 --> 06:01.444
Have you ever even lived in an apartment?

06:01.944 --> 06:04.364
You're used to the house.
It's gonna get stuffy in here.

06:04.906 --> 06:07.617
Where do we hang laundry?
Where do we put the fermenting jars?

06:07.700 --> 06:10.203
I didn't live in houses
because I preferred to.

06:10.828 --> 06:14.332
I don't mind if it's a stuffy apartment
or your parents' spare room.

06:15.375 --> 06:17.668
You are my home. That's enough for me.

06:18.753 --> 06:19.837
[groans]

06:20.797 --> 06:22.340
You should've married a rich man.

06:22.423 --> 06:25.510
You love dressing up nice.
You love reading books.

06:25.593 --> 06:26.761
[chuckles]

06:26.844 --> 06:28.554
You were born to be a rich man's wife.

06:30.139 --> 06:31.557
What are you saying?

06:31.641 --> 06:33.893
All the wives of Dodong-ri
will be jealous.

06:33.976 --> 06:36.396
Just look at this garden I have.

06:36.479 --> 06:37.814
[laughing]

06:41.234 --> 06:44.320
Where did you get this wallpaper?
It's so old-fashioned.

06:45.238 --> 06:47.990
[Geum-myeong] The road ahead
could be a million miles long…

06:48.074 --> 06:49.909
[middle-aged Gwan-sik]
Stop, you'll make a mess.

06:51.119 --> 06:53.746
[Geum-myeong] But the greatest joy
you will ever have

06:53.830 --> 06:55.248
is the one in front of you.

06:55.331 --> 06:56.874
[feel-good music playing]

06:56.958 --> 06:58.668
[woman 5]
You gave your daughter everything,

06:58.751 --> 07:00.837
so now it's back to street vending.

07:01.921 --> 07:05.842
[sighs] Jeez.
You're as stubborn as Gwang-rye.

07:06.342 --> 07:08.761
You could've let us maintain
the previous name at least.

07:08.845 --> 07:10.012
AUNTIES' SEAFOOD HOUSE

07:10.096 --> 07:13.182
[middle-aged Ae-sun] Why should my name
be up there? I didn't pay for it.

07:13.266 --> 07:15.393
I would never accept it. Never, ever.

07:15.476 --> 07:16.394
[chuckles]

07:16.477 --> 07:18.146
Tell me,
since you have years of experience,

07:18.229 --> 07:20.148
has pride ever put food on the table?

07:20.231 --> 07:22.900
I wouldn't invest this much
in something that doesn't pay.

07:22.984 --> 07:25.278
-[middle-aged Ae-sun sighs]
-[woman 5 laughs]

07:25.361 --> 07:27.864
Anyway, you better not waive
my vendor fee.

07:27.947 --> 07:29.699
I'll pay full price like anyone else.

07:29.782 --> 07:32.702
And before you get any ideas,
I'll just sell tsukidashi, okay?

07:32.785 --> 07:34.745
Don't dare try to slip me
any of your inventory.

07:34.829 --> 07:36.330
[woman 5] Goodness.

07:36.414 --> 07:37.915
[middle-aged Ae-sun gasps] Oh!

07:37.999 --> 07:40.376
What's the matter with you? I've had it!

07:40.460 --> 07:43.254
You can't do your schoolwork,
but you have time to play with that ball?

07:43.337 --> 07:45.214
-I'm sorry.
-Your hair.

07:45.298 --> 07:47.258
What's with that? Who paid for that?

07:47.341 --> 07:48.301
[Eun-myeong] I dunno.

07:48.384 --> 07:50.970
You're selling that
superstitious stuff again, aren't you?

07:51.053 --> 07:52.680
Oh my. Oh my. What the--

07:52.763 --> 07:55.808
Oh, I've had enough! You make me so mad!

07:55.892 --> 07:57.185
-I can't stand it!
-What did I do?

07:57.268 --> 07:58.728
[woman 5] It's soaking wet.

07:59.228 --> 08:02.899
[Gyeong-ja] Turn off the faucet. Hurry.
Poor Ae-sun's clock is destroyed.

08:02.982 --> 08:05.610
[woman 5] Hey, careful, careful.
Watch your hand.

08:11.741 --> 08:14.869
He left before dinner.
Where did he go? [sighs]

08:15.578 --> 08:17.163
Probably at Cheol-yong's again.

08:18.873 --> 08:19.916
[sighs]

08:19.999 --> 08:23.377
There's nothing as comforting
as a young child, is there?

08:24.879 --> 08:28.090
No matter what,
they always come running back to Mommy.

08:29.634 --> 08:31.511
Don't be too hard on the kid.

08:32.094 --> 08:36.098
A leaf can be torn apart
even in a gentle drizzle.

08:41.270 --> 08:44.273
Oh, Auntie, when will I grow up finally?

08:45.983 --> 08:47.568
When I do, I'll let you know.

08:48.486 --> 08:51.489
[Geum-myeong] It turns out
none of us have it all figured out.

08:51.989 --> 08:55.034
[woman 5] You bought a big one.
Why would you do that, I wonder?

08:55.117 --> 08:59.330
[laughs] Could it possibly be your way
of asking us to be good to your wife?

08:59.413 --> 09:00.540
-Yes.
-[Gyeong-ja laughs]

09:00.623 --> 09:04.168
Boy, your people skills
have come a long way. [laughs]

09:05.836 --> 09:09.215
[Geum-myeong] Every time I felt my heart
aching with growing pains,

09:09.715 --> 09:12.510
the hearts around me
were growing a little bit too.

09:15.763 --> 09:17.306
-I'm coming!
-[Gyeong-ja] Do that later.

09:17.390 --> 09:19.934
-[middle-aged Ae-sun] Button up your vest.
-Don't bother, dear.

09:20.017 --> 09:22.353
-Okay, where would you like us to stand?
-You want me here?

09:22.436 --> 09:24.188
-Ready?
-[Gyeong-ja] Look. Come to the middle.

09:24.272 --> 09:25.439
Hey, come here.

09:25.940 --> 09:27.733
-Okay, is everything ready?
-Wait one second.

09:27.817 --> 09:28.985
-Ow, come on.
-One second.

09:29.068 --> 09:30.778
-Hold still. Hey.
-Leave my hair alone.

09:30.861 --> 09:34.115
[middle-aged Gwan-sik] One, two, kimchi!

09:35.241 --> 09:36.701
[camera shutter clicks]

09:37.577 --> 09:38.953
[woman on recording] Lesson five.

09:39.036 --> 09:42.331
In this lesson, we will learn
how to talk about the weather.

09:42.915 --> 09:45.334
-Please listen to the following example.
-[Geum-myeong sobs]

09:46.627 --> 09:48.546
Yesterday, it was cold.

09:48.629 --> 09:50.631
[woman speaking Japanese]

09:50.715 --> 09:51.841
[Geum-myeong sobs]

09:51.924 --> 09:55.678
[woman in English]
Today, it's 30 degrees. It's very hot.

09:55.761 --> 09:58.431
[sobs]

09:58.931 --> 10:00.016
[sniffles]

10:00.099 --> 10:01.642
[woman speaking Japanese]

10:02.768 --> 10:03.644
[groans]

10:03.728 --> 10:06.814
[Geum-myeong in English] Come on, Mom.
I told you to stop street vending.

10:06.897 --> 10:10.318
I hate how you have to eat sitting out
on the street there every day.

10:11.611 --> 10:13.070
What did she write here?

10:13.154 --> 10:14.280
COME AND CHECK US OUT!

10:14.363 --> 10:17.283
[woman on recording]
Today, it's 30 degrees. It's very hot.

10:17.366 --> 10:20.369
FRESH FISH DAILY, STRAIGHT FROM THE BOAT
MARKET PRICES ALL DAY

10:20.453 --> 10:23.331
[crying]

10:26.042 --> 10:29.754
[Geum-myeong] Sometimes, your heart
grows so much, it feels like bursting.

10:29.837 --> 10:33.215
When I realized Mom was street vending
again because of me,

10:33.299 --> 10:34.759
I made a resolution.

10:38.554 --> 10:39.722
I resolved

10:40.348 --> 10:41.599
that I would never again

10:42.725 --> 10:45.061
let my parents be robbed of their dreams.

10:45.144 --> 10:47.396
[upbeat disco music playing]

10:47.480 --> 10:51.067
SONG YEONG-SAM
SAN-108, BONGCHEON 5-DONG

10:55.404 --> 10:57.490
Rent for places closer to school
must be expensive.

10:57.573 --> 10:59.325
FARAWAY NATIONS AND NEIGHBORING NATIONS

10:59.408 --> 11:00.951
It's not so bad to live downhill.

11:01.577 --> 11:03.287
The climb is good for your health.

11:03.371 --> 11:04.830
INTEREST RATE SOARS
JAPAN'S ECONOMY UNSTABLE

11:04.914 --> 11:08.626
Would it… would it be possible
to fix the door lock, um, sir?

11:15.675 --> 11:18.260
[man] It's just my kid on the other side.
What's the big deal?

11:19.345 --> 11:23.641
I know, but if you could even put up
a hook-latch, that would be enough.

11:25.059 --> 11:27.103
[man] What, do you not trust us?

11:27.186 --> 11:29.397
Hmm? You're a funny one.
I'll give you that.

11:30.147 --> 11:33.317
You know, the girl who lived here
before you never said a thing.

11:33.401 --> 11:36.320
She just thought our baby was cute.
She couldn't get enough.

11:36.404 --> 11:38.155
Just look at him. Look, look.

11:38.239 --> 11:40.199
-[TV] We need Yeong-sim!
-He's adorable!

11:40.700 --> 11:42.535
-Please!
-[Geum-myeong] Yeah.

11:43.160 --> 11:45.329
-We need Yeong-sim. Please!
-[boy laughs]

11:45.871 --> 11:47.248
Cute boy. Mm.

11:48.332 --> 11:51.544
Really, you should know how hard it is
to find a room for rent these days,

11:51.627 --> 11:53.379
even harder than finding an apartment.

11:53.879 --> 11:57.883
As far as tenants go, we have plenty
of options, but you, not so much.

11:59.468 --> 12:03.305
YEONG-SIM
YEONG-SIM'S DREAM

12:04.932 --> 12:07.852
Let's just go easy on each other
and try to get along.

12:08.436 --> 12:10.646
Sure, if you say so.

12:12.773 --> 12:14.984
It's not like I have another choice.

12:15.067 --> 12:18.446
Also, I say this
because I have a daughter your age.

12:18.529 --> 12:19.864
No boyfriends allowed.

12:19.947 --> 12:23.159
-Not even one.
-Not even Park Chung-seop.

12:23.242 --> 12:25.578
If you were my daughter,
I'd break your legs if I caught you.

12:25.661 --> 12:27.955
If I were your daughter,
you'd put up a hook-latch.

12:28.038 --> 12:31.125
DO NOT ENTER! KNOCK!

12:31.208 --> 12:32.543
[phone line ringing]

12:38.758 --> 12:40.134
[zipper zips]

12:40.217 --> 12:41.469
Sh, sh.

12:42.136 --> 12:43.929
[zipper zips]

12:44.013 --> 12:46.223
Hey, quiet. You wanna get caught?

12:48.267 --> 12:50.269
[jaunty music playing]

12:53.063 --> 12:53.981
Hi there.

12:55.232 --> 12:56.275
Cheol-yong's here.

12:57.109 --> 12:58.277
That's right, your son.

12:58.778 --> 12:59.653
Uh-huh.

13:01.739 --> 13:04.992
MacGyver is on right now,
but my son isn't coming out of his room.

13:06.035 --> 13:07.036
Yeah.

13:07.119 --> 13:08.245
Sure thing.

13:09.830 --> 13:11.791
I can't believe Cheol-yong would do this.

13:11.874 --> 13:14.168
If he was so afraid of
his dad yelling at him,

13:14.251 --> 13:16.462
he shouldn't have
finished last in his class.

13:17.087 --> 13:20.049
So now, not only is he last,
he's a runaway too!

13:20.132 --> 13:20.966
[knocking at door]

13:21.050 --> 13:22.802
[music fades]

13:32.853 --> 13:34.355
[middle-aged Ae-sun clears throat]

13:37.650 --> 13:38.984
[exhales sharply]

13:42.988 --> 13:44.990
[jaunty music resumes]

13:47.201 --> 13:48.786
Why did you lock the door, son?

13:48.869 --> 13:50.079
P… privacy.

13:50.913 --> 13:52.414
[scoffs] P… I'm sorry?

13:52.498 --> 13:54.834
Privacy. It means get out of my room!

13:56.502 --> 13:59.964
So now it's your room, eh?
You didn't buy this place though.

14:00.047 --> 14:01.423
So what?

14:01.507 --> 14:05.261
That's all you've had to say to me lately.
"So what?" It's annoying.

14:06.637 --> 14:09.223
Come on, get out already!
You just don't understand.

14:09.306 --> 14:10.599
[middle-aged Ae-sun] Excuse me?

14:14.979 --> 14:15.896
[grunts]

14:18.190 --> 14:20.067
[woman] So what do we do now? You tell me.

14:22.194 --> 14:24.446
What am I supposed to do
if you won't talk to me?

14:27.074 --> 14:28.742
Fine, let's just break up.

14:28.826 --> 14:31.161
You don't love me anymore.
Not enough to even shave for me.

14:31.245 --> 14:34.206
[man 2] It's not because I don't love you.
I can't stop loving you.

14:34.290 --> 14:36.750
-I don't even know how!
-[woman] Then what are you gonna do?

14:36.834 --> 14:39.169
Quit your job and take
the teacher certification exam.

14:39.253 --> 14:40.713
I can't just marry anyone.

14:40.796 --> 14:43.591
I definitely can't marry a bum.
What are your paintings worth?

14:43.674 --> 14:45.509
Why are those more important than I am?

14:45.593 --> 14:48.178
[sighs] I should ask him
to soundproof it next.

14:48.262 --> 14:51.265
[woman] How am I supposed to convince
my dad about you? Can you at least shave?

14:51.348 --> 14:53.058
Am I worth less to you
than your facial hair?

14:53.142 --> 14:54.476
[door rattles in distance]

14:55.477 --> 14:57.563
Oh, make sure to give me the biggest one.

14:57.646 --> 14:59.148
Give Bu-seon the smallest one.

14:59.231 --> 15:00.274
[man] Sure.

15:04.361 --> 15:05.195
Huh?

15:07.114 --> 15:09.158
Somebody took the key, Dad.

15:10.117 --> 15:11.452
Bu-seon, are you in there?

15:12.161 --> 15:14.330
-Bu-seon!
-Bu-seon!

15:16.373 --> 15:17.499
Song Bu-seon!

15:21.128 --> 15:22.713
[grunting]

15:23.380 --> 15:25.090
-Oh my.
-How dare he.

15:25.591 --> 15:28.510
[whispers] He's just a teenager, remember?
A teenager.

15:28.594 --> 15:30.721
Yeah? So what?
That doesn't give him a pass.

15:30.804 --> 15:31.639
Just think.

15:31.722 --> 15:34.934
Remember you would bring me croakers
when you shouldn't have.

15:36.310 --> 15:39.438
Your mom wanted to
shove your head in dirty dishwater.

15:39.521 --> 15:40.773
[groans]

15:42.775 --> 15:43.651
Here.

15:45.027 --> 15:48.030
So… I can handle my mom.

15:48.906 --> 15:49.865
No problem.

15:57.039 --> 15:57.873
Hang on.

15:59.416 --> 16:00.501
Why are there two forks?

16:02.753 --> 16:04.004
Why did Mom give me two forks?

16:04.964 --> 16:05.839
[banging at door]

16:08.801 --> 16:09.635
Bu-seon!

16:10.886 --> 16:12.721
-Song Bu-seon!
-[sighs]

16:12.805 --> 16:15.099
-This is the wrong place for me, I think.
-Open the door.

16:15.182 --> 16:16.767
[banging at door]

16:17.393 --> 16:19.269
-What are you doing?
-What are you doing?

16:19.353 --> 16:21.397
-Song Bu-seon!
-Song Bu-seon!

16:22.064 --> 16:24.024
[man] Hey, Song Bu-seon! Open the door!

16:24.900 --> 16:26.110
-[thud]
-[gasps]

16:28.278 --> 16:29.113
[man] Bu-seon!

16:29.196 --> 16:30.614
[banging at door continues]

16:30.698 --> 16:33.075
-[man] Hey, open the door!
-[boy] Open the door!

16:33.158 --> 16:34.743
-[man] Open the door!
-[gasps] Oh my God.

16:34.827 --> 16:36.662
-[man] Open it!
-[Geum-myeong] Oh my God.

16:37.538 --> 16:38.372
[man] Open it!

16:38.872 --> 16:40.124
Who… who… who are you?

16:40.207 --> 16:42.459
-[grunts]
-[Bu-seon] Oh my God!

16:43.127 --> 16:45.462
[breathing heavily]

16:47.047 --> 16:48.340
[man] Open the door!

16:49.049 --> 16:51.385
Oh my God! Are you insane?

16:51.468 --> 16:53.220
What do you think you're doing?

16:59.268 --> 17:00.436
[man] Hey!

17:00.519 --> 17:02.354
Open the door!

17:03.397 --> 17:04.231
[Bu-seon] Hey!

17:05.858 --> 17:08.944
Listen, could you help us out
this one time?

17:09.028 --> 17:10.946
Please, my dad will kill us.

17:11.030 --> 17:12.406
-[man] Song Bu-seon!
-Please help.

17:12.489 --> 17:13.866
[boy] Song Bu-seon!

17:13.949 --> 17:15.701
-Please help me.
-[man] Open the door!

17:15.784 --> 17:17.911
[Geum-myeong] The look
in this hairy boy's eyes

17:18.495 --> 17:21.623
made me think of a mole
that's been cornered by a hunter.

17:21.707 --> 17:23.542
[whimpers]

17:24.501 --> 17:26.503
[intriguing music playing]

17:27.921 --> 17:29.298
So I let him in.

17:29.381 --> 17:31.925
[Yeong-sim on TV] Yay! Wow!
Geum-sun just won!

17:32.009 --> 17:33.218
[laughs]

17:36.430 --> 17:37.681
[Bu-seon] So, Dad, I, uh…

17:39.641 --> 17:40.642
Don't get up.

17:41.393 --> 17:43.687
I made some jjinbbang. Thought I'd share.

17:44.188 --> 17:46.940
I wanted to see how you were settling in.

17:47.024 --> 17:49.777
[clears throat] It's just… you're early.

17:49.860 --> 17:53.238
I thought you'd be
working at the factory today.

17:53.322 --> 17:55.449
Since when are you interested
in what I do?

17:56.200 --> 17:58.911
You have a pretty big closet here,
don't you?

17:58.994 --> 18:00.329
Dad, what about dinner?

18:01.205 --> 18:03.874
[Bu-seon's dad] This is the perfect size
for your blankets, huh?

18:03.957 --> 18:05.876
Uh, yeah, I suppose it is.

18:08.796 --> 18:09.963
[Geum-myeong sighs]

18:11.173 --> 18:12.424
What do you mean you "suppose"?

18:12.508 --> 18:16.720
You know what?
I think I will go outside for a bit.

18:16.804 --> 18:17.930
What about that one?

18:19.139 --> 18:21.058
You using the extra storage?

18:21.725 --> 18:24.436
-Yeah, I…
-Uh, Dad, she said she's stepping out, so…

18:24.520 --> 18:26.188
Oh, uh, hold on, sir.

18:26.271 --> 18:28.440
I keep my underwear in there. [chuckles]

18:29.191 --> 18:32.194
No need to see all that.
[chuckles nervously]

18:35.197 --> 18:38.450
As I said, I think I'll go out.

18:39.493 --> 18:41.453
Yeah. Okay, sure.

18:46.250 --> 18:48.127
What are you hanging around here for?

18:49.253 --> 18:50.504
[Bu-seon] Oh, uh…

18:50.587 --> 18:52.297
No, I wasn't. I… I just

18:53.132 --> 18:56.301
was wondering who the new tenant was.
That's all.

18:56.385 --> 18:58.428
Well, that's odd
'cause you've never cared before.

18:59.221 --> 19:01.640
You only care about
your freedom and your boyfriends.

19:03.100 --> 19:04.810
Dad, it's not like that.

19:06.311 --> 19:07.354
Come out.

19:08.647 --> 19:10.274
Come out right now.

19:10.357 --> 19:11.775
-[Bu-seon] Dad, listen.
-Mr. Song.

19:11.859 --> 19:12.901
Really, it's not--

19:12.985 --> 19:15.404
You either walk out or I drag you out.

19:15.487 --> 19:16.780
Right now.

19:18.115 --> 19:19.366
Cheol-yong, come out.

19:19.449 --> 19:22.494
Oh, we said we'd take it easy.

19:22.578 --> 19:23.745
Park Cheol-yong.

19:25.497 --> 19:26.331
Come out.

19:26.415 --> 19:27.499
Park Chung-seop!

19:27.583 --> 19:29.168
Park Chung-seop!

19:34.047 --> 19:35.090
[funky music playing]

19:35.174 --> 19:37.551
[Geum-myeong] When Grandma Min-ok
turned 60, she said,

19:39.469 --> 19:41.930
"Anyone who claims to be a moral person

19:42.014 --> 19:44.766
probably has a few skeletons
hiding in the closet."

19:50.230 --> 19:51.315
Excuse me?

19:54.526 --> 19:55.777
Could you, uh…

20:07.122 --> 20:08.207
I'm sorry.

20:10.250 --> 20:11.376
I'm sorry.

20:13.462 --> 20:16.173
[Geum-myeong] Sure, it was embarrassing,

20:16.673 --> 20:18.425
but that was the day we first met.

20:22.471 --> 20:25.057
[middle-aged Gwan-sik] I knew it!
Cheol-yong, you little punk.

20:25.641 --> 20:27.601
Your father lost his nails, you know that?

20:27.684 --> 20:29.895
Your father works his fingers
to the bone at the market.

20:30.395 --> 20:32.064
-How dare you run away from home!
-Honey.

20:32.147 --> 20:32.981
How…

20:33.482 --> 20:34.358
Hold on.

20:34.441 --> 20:36.151
[music fades]

20:40.280 --> 20:41.448
Did he get smaller?

20:43.367 --> 20:44.284
How is he smaller?

20:51.416 --> 20:52.584
Cheol-yong?

21:10.519 --> 21:11.353
Who are you?

21:11.937 --> 21:13.188
[Hyeon-suk coughs]

21:17.150 --> 21:17.985
Wait.

21:18.568 --> 21:20.404
-[Hyeon-suk coughs]
-Are you a girl?

21:23.991 --> 21:25.867
[jaunty music playing]

21:25.951 --> 21:27.035
Oh my God.

21:51.560 --> 21:54.730
[middle-aged Gwan-sik sighs] So, uh…

21:56.189 --> 21:57.274
That haircut.

21:58.150 --> 21:59.443
Did you do that yourself?

22:00.569 --> 22:02.112
Has money been tight?

22:02.195 --> 22:03.280
Actually,

22:04.281 --> 22:05.490
my parents did this.

22:08.452 --> 22:10.203
[middle-aged Ae-sun sighs]

22:10.287 --> 22:12.164
So I was wondering.

22:13.373 --> 22:18.503
Those letters.
Does YEM stand for "Yang Eun-myeong"?

22:19.254 --> 22:20.255
Yes, it does.

22:20.339 --> 22:23.425
[middle-aged Ae-sun] Why are
my son's initials on your backpack?

22:23.508 --> 22:25.302
Are you close to each other?

22:27.137 --> 22:28.055
Are you?

22:28.638 --> 22:29.639
She's my girlfriend.

22:32.684 --> 22:33.602
Oh my God.

22:35.020 --> 22:37.898
-It's been 500 days.
-Where the hell did I put that paddle?

22:38.648 --> 22:40.317
This bastard needs 500 spankings!

22:40.400 --> 22:42.152
[Eun-myeong] You dated
in elementary school.

22:42.235 --> 22:45.072
-We were older than that!
-Who… who told you that, son?

22:45.155 --> 22:48.325
-Aunt Gyeong-ok.
-Ah! Tell Yang Gyeong-ok to get here now!

22:48.408 --> 22:49.451
Love isn't illegal!

22:49.534 --> 22:51.036
What did you just say, boy?

22:51.870 --> 22:53.538
[Gwan-sik] There's an outcry with no sound

22:54.122 --> 22:56.249
An eternal handkerchief of nostalgia

22:56.750 --> 22:59.086
That waves
That waves towards the blue sea

22:59.169 --> 23:01.088
The first man hanging in the air…

23:02.422 --> 23:03.465
We didn't rush into it.

23:04.091 --> 23:05.759
At first, I didn't even like her

23:06.510 --> 23:08.303
because of the hair on her upper lip.

23:08.804 --> 23:11.181
But… but after ten years,
it suddenly didn't matter anymore.

23:12.641 --> 23:13.975
What was I supposed to do?

23:14.059 --> 23:17.354
[moans] Oh God.
I don't wanna hear any of this! Stop it!

23:17.437 --> 23:19.564
This family just treats me
like an afterthought!

23:19.648 --> 23:21.900
But she loved me
more than anything in the world.

23:21.983 --> 23:23.443
More than her brothers, even!

23:24.820 --> 23:26.154
[middle-aged Ae-sun sighs]

23:27.531 --> 23:29.866
I hope you're happy now, dummy.

23:29.950 --> 23:31.034
Congrats.

23:31.118 --> 23:34.329
[Geum-myeong] Yang Eun-myeong's weakness
for love was just like Dad's.

23:34.413 --> 23:39.334
The thing is,
I've always had a thing for bad boys, so…

23:46.091 --> 23:50.011
Listen, young lady, being in love
doesn't excuse running away. You get that?

23:50.720 --> 23:52.139
Your mom and dad, do they know?

23:52.848 --> 23:54.433
They wouldn't know yet.

23:56.309 --> 23:58.311
I only left home this morning, so…

23:58.395 --> 24:00.564
Why don't you tell us who you are, dear?

24:01.064 --> 24:02.441
Let's start with your name.

24:03.316 --> 24:04.609
Tell me, what is it?

24:06.027 --> 24:07.112
Hyeon-suk.

24:08.697 --> 24:10.991
I think Hyeon-suk can speak for herself.

24:16.163 --> 24:17.622
Bu Hyeon-suk.

24:22.419 --> 24:23.420
Hello there.

24:24.004 --> 24:25.797
[upbeat pop music playing]

24:25.881 --> 24:26.840
[exhales sharply]

24:27.424 --> 24:29.843
"Bu" Hyeon-suk.
Does that mean your father is

24:30.760 --> 24:31.595
Bu Sang-gil?

24:34.139 --> 24:34.973
Yeah.

24:35.640 --> 24:37.225
[whimpers] Oh my God.

24:37.309 --> 24:41.354
[Gyeong-ja] How can a love scandal
span two generations? It's a small town.

24:41.438 --> 24:43.440
[woman 5] It extended
to a second generation

24:43.523 --> 24:45.525
precisely because it's a small town.

24:45.609 --> 24:47.486
I'm just shocked they're the same age.

24:47.569 --> 24:51.740
I didn't get to bring you kimchi
or visit when you were moving.

24:53.158 --> 24:55.285
[Gyeong-ja] When you met each other
for the first time,

24:55.368 --> 24:57.621
you must both have been
pregnant with them.

24:58.955 --> 25:01.583
Hyeon-suk, never step on a pile of poop.

25:01.666 --> 25:05.045
You have to marry a man
like this lady's husband, okay?

25:07.297 --> 25:10.467
Hyeon-suk is also going to
Dodong Elementary, right?

25:10.550 --> 25:12.552
[woman 5] There are only
so many people in a grade,

25:12.636 --> 25:15.096
and they had ten years of school
to figure it out.

25:16.223 --> 25:19.684
[man] You cared so much for your daughter
that you completely neglected your son.

25:19.768 --> 25:22.103
Do you even know what kind of students
he's hanging out with?

25:22.187 --> 25:26.066
[woman 5] Considering the odds,
it's actually not that surprising.

25:26.566 --> 25:29.027
We have a female student
who's as much trouble as he is!

25:29.110 --> 25:32.197
He wouldn't have anything
to do with girls, sir.

25:33.073 --> 25:35.784
He doesn't know how
to get along with them.

25:37.327 --> 25:39.746
He can't even get along
with his own sister.

25:40.330 --> 25:43.208
Sisters are different.
Even I can't hang out with my sister.

25:44.584 --> 25:45.418
Oh.

25:45.502 --> 25:46.586
[sighs]

25:49.130 --> 25:51.132
[upbeat pop music continues]

26:10.402 --> 26:12.904
[Gyeong-ja] I think this is about
more than chance.

26:12.988 --> 26:14.447
I think this is about taste.

26:14.531 --> 26:17.325
He must take after his father. [laughs]

26:17.867 --> 26:21.413
What can I say?
Indecency seems to run in the Oh family.

26:24.124 --> 26:26.001
Just have a look
at my own daughters instead.

26:26.084 --> 26:29.296
Hyeon-suk, which stands for
"wise and enlightened," and Jeong-suk,

26:30.213 --> 26:32.424
which stands for "silent."

26:36.303 --> 26:37.220
[sighs]

26:43.226 --> 26:45.186
Bu Hyeon-suk, come out right now!

26:50.692 --> 26:52.235
At least come inside and say hello.

26:52.319 --> 26:53.528
What, are they getting engaged?

26:53.612 --> 26:55.447
[Gyeong-ja] If you ask me,

26:55.530 --> 26:58.658
I think Bu Sang-gil still has
a bit of a crush on Ae-sun.

26:58.742 --> 27:00.035
How dare he!

27:00.118 --> 27:02.329
AUNTIES' SEAFOOD HOUSE

27:02.412 --> 27:04.456
I'm sure of it. [laughs]

27:05.040 --> 27:07.125
[laughter]

27:07.208 --> 27:08.793
Passion is inherited too.

27:08.877 --> 27:11.755
Everybody in your family
is obsessed with romance.

27:12.339 --> 27:13.632
You're having fun, aren't you?

27:13.715 --> 27:15.175
What are you upset about?

27:15.258 --> 27:16.426
Come on.

27:16.509 --> 27:18.219
Do you have the right to be upset?

27:19.095 --> 27:19.929
Do you?

27:20.013 --> 27:23.600
You did some wild things
in your own youth, as I recall.

27:23.683 --> 27:26.353
You just can't stop
the spring from coming, remember?

27:26.436 --> 27:30.190
Even for you, it was spring, wasn't it?

27:30.690 --> 27:33.652
For once in her life,
my daughter-in-law is speechless!

27:33.735 --> 27:34.611
[laughs]

27:34.694 --> 27:36.863
-Oh, you!
-Well, you seem very happy about it.

27:36.946 --> 27:39.115
Like you've waited for this moment
your whole life.

27:39.199 --> 27:41.034
Ae-sun, you better watch out.

27:41.117 --> 27:43.244
You could lose your own son
just the same way.

27:43.328 --> 27:46.247
Watch it. He is still your grandson.

27:46.331 --> 27:48.291
[laughing]

27:48.917 --> 27:55.590
[in Korean] ♪ My strawberry-like innocence
At 18 ♪

27:56.216 --> 28:00.011
♪ If my own mom doesn't understand me
What should I do? ♪

28:00.095 --> 28:01.721
[in English] Oh goodness.

28:02.472 --> 28:03.973
What, are you a singer now?

28:04.933 --> 28:06.184
Turn this thing off!

28:07.143 --> 28:10.397
[TV] President Roh Tae-woo has declared
war on crime and violence.

28:10.480 --> 28:12.982
Even in wartimes, there's a place to rest.

28:13.483 --> 28:17.237
Eventually, flowers grow,
and snowfall covers the old battlefields.

28:18.196 --> 28:19.406
Leave them alone.

28:19.989 --> 28:21.700
Let the kids do what they must.

28:21.783 --> 28:24.953
…the Hwaseong serial murders
as well as a wave of human trafficking…

28:25.036 --> 28:27.831
[woman 6] They're in the springtime
of their lives right now.

28:27.914 --> 28:30.709
["Unchained Melody" playing]

28:30.792 --> 28:32.585
GHOST
NOVEMBER 24, CANNES THEATER

28:37.173 --> 28:38.550
RACETRACK PART-TIME JOB

28:39.050 --> 28:41.970
SALES ASSISTANT WANTED

28:43.596 --> 28:46.433
EXCHANGE STUDENT IN TOKYO
LOOKING FOR JAPANESE TRANSLATION JOBS

28:46.516 --> 28:48.393
CLASS OF '87, ENGLISH LITERATURE
YANG GEUM-MYEONG

28:48.476 --> 28:50.395
[Geum-myeong] Unlike what you see on TV,

28:50.478 --> 28:52.939
I wasn't suddenly rich
because I'd studied abroad.

28:53.022 --> 28:54.315
KOREAN-JAPANESE TUTOR

28:54.983 --> 28:58.695
Jeez, why did these kids
have to hang their posters next to mine?

28:59.320 --> 29:00.697
[Geum-myeong] In those days,

29:00.780 --> 29:04.159
it felt like my life
was moving at a glacial pace.

29:06.828 --> 29:09.706
You can put up posters
on your own time, huh?

29:10.415 --> 29:13.418
Like, if you hit your quota,
can you do it whenever?

29:22.802 --> 29:25.054
-Oh.
-Oh, hello again.

29:25.138 --> 29:26.347
[sighs]

29:29.851 --> 29:33.855
So do you want a part-time job?
Is that right?

29:34.856 --> 29:36.858
Uh-huh. I do. [chuckles]

29:36.941 --> 29:38.318
Well,

29:39.360 --> 29:40.361
this is my job.

29:41.112 --> 29:42.155
Ah.

29:42.238 --> 29:45.825
My job involves anything
related to painting.

29:45.909 --> 29:47.243
Okay.

29:47.994 --> 29:48.828
Well,

29:49.871 --> 29:50.872
go ahead.

29:50.955 --> 29:52.707
♪ Lonely rivers flow ♪

29:53.500 --> 29:56.878
♪ To the sea, to the sea ♪

29:57.629 --> 30:00.089
♪ To the open arms… ♪

30:00.173 --> 30:01.508
GHOST

30:01.591 --> 30:04.844
GHOST
CANNES THEATER

30:04.928 --> 30:07.889
♪ Lonely rivers sigh ♪

30:07.972 --> 30:11.559
♪ "Wait for me, wait for me" ♪

30:12.143 --> 30:14.479
♪ I'll be coming home… ♪

30:14.562 --> 30:16.064
[man] Listen up, everyone.

30:16.898 --> 30:20.568
Ghost will start at 7:00 p.m.
at Cannes Theater.

30:21.861 --> 30:23.404
[man on recording] Chapter Three.

30:23.488 --> 30:24.948
PART-TIME USHER
CANNES THEATER

30:25.824 --> 30:29.536
Department heads wear academic robes
at the college on the hill.

30:32.372 --> 30:35.834
In Chapter Three, even in the US,
they first wear their…

30:35.917 --> 30:40.255
[man 2] Explain something to me, kid.
Why does Ong-nyeo have all her clothes on?

30:42.465 --> 30:44.259
It's a skin flick poster,
for crying out loud.

30:44.342 --> 30:45.176
BYEON KANG-SOE 3

30:45.260 --> 30:47.262
You think you're Picasso or something?

30:47.345 --> 30:50.473
People come to see Ong-nyeo
for one thing only.

30:50.557 --> 30:53.852
They don't come here to see
some landscape that you painted.

30:53.935 --> 30:56.229
Paint for Piccadilly.
Paint for Danseongsa.

30:56.896 --> 30:59.816
In my theater,
I expect to see a little bare leg.

30:59.899 --> 31:04.112
[sighs] Why do you insist on making
your own art with other people's money?

31:04.195 --> 31:05.780
Huh? The paint? Did you buy it?

31:05.864 --> 31:08.575
Did I give you this basement
as your personal gallery?

31:09.742 --> 31:11.536
I choose to express the joys and sorrows

31:11.619 --> 31:13.788
of Ong-nyeo's affairs
against these mountains.

31:13.872 --> 31:16.124
What about my joys and sorrows?

31:16.624 --> 31:19.460
You're putting me through
more ups and downs than her!

31:20.461 --> 31:22.547
A painting isn't a photograph. It--

31:22.630 --> 31:24.757
[in Korean] Look here, Mr. Park.

31:24.841 --> 31:27.635
No, Lord Artist. Your Majesty of Art.

31:28.303 --> 31:29.762
[in English] I'm not asking for much.

31:29.846 --> 31:32.807
I'm asking you to help me out
for once in your life.

31:32.891 --> 31:34.058
[vehicle horn honks]

31:36.477 --> 31:38.396
-Wanna come see a movie?
-No. I don't think so.

31:38.479 --> 31:42.692
Oh, it's that scalper lady.
Lady! I told you to get out of here!

31:42.775 --> 31:45.194
You're not allowed to resell our tickets!

31:45.278 --> 31:46.863
[woman] He's our very own Picasso.

31:46.946 --> 31:49.532
We have a Picasso
in the basement of Cannes Theater.

31:50.033 --> 31:53.494
Never raises his voice,
but he's stubborn as a bull. [grunts]

31:53.578 --> 31:55.830
He always keeps his eyes down
when he gets caught,

31:55.914 --> 31:57.457
but he just goes and does it again.

31:57.540 --> 32:00.752
The boss has been more than patient
with him. I would've gone crazy.

32:00.835 --> 32:02.545
So he's an actual artist, is he, huh?

32:02.629 --> 32:04.172
I suppose he is.

32:04.255 --> 32:06.925
As much as anyone who paints
a billboard anonymously can be.

32:07.008 --> 32:08.968
Hmm. But he hasn't been fired yet.

32:09.552 --> 32:10.678
The boss is a softy.

32:10.762 --> 32:11.763
Huh?

32:11.846 --> 32:12.889
After he yells at him,

32:12.972 --> 32:15.141
he ends up feeling so badly,
he buys the kid some dinner.

32:16.142 --> 32:17.310
Uh-huh. [chuckles]

32:17.393 --> 32:19.771
[alarm clock ringing]

32:23.524 --> 32:27.528
So how do you know each other?
Why did he introduce you to us?

32:27.612 --> 32:29.405
[Geum-myeong] Oh, I met him somewhere.

32:29.489 --> 32:30.865
[customer] Two tickets, please.

32:30.949 --> 32:34.202
That's how it goes.
You meet a guy, then you end up with him.

32:34.953 --> 32:36.412
-What?
-[laughs]

32:39.332 --> 32:42.168
["Jingle Bells" instrumental playing]

32:42.961 --> 32:43.795
[Geum-myeong] Next.

32:43.878 --> 32:45.380
TELL US THE NAME OF THE MOVIE

32:46.339 --> 32:47.840
[customer 2] One ticket, please.

32:50.468 --> 32:51.594
Next customer.

32:52.512 --> 32:53.471
TICKET
GHOST

32:53.554 --> 32:55.556
-[Yeong-beom] Excuse me.
-How many?

32:55.640 --> 32:57.141
I'm not here for Ghost.

32:57.225 --> 32:59.852
Byeon Kang-soe is later at night.
Next customer.

32:59.936 --> 33:02.271
-[Yeong-beom] Have you seen it?
-Next customer.

33:02.355 --> 33:03.982
[Yeong-beom] Come see it with me later.

33:04.732 --> 33:06.150
Are you gonna buy a ticket?

33:09.570 --> 33:10.530
[coin clatters]

33:13.032 --> 33:14.033
[sighs]

33:15.159 --> 33:17.787
I suppose crazy people
buy movie tickets too.

33:18.538 --> 33:19.539
[scoffs]

33:20.206 --> 33:21.082
What the…

33:36.973 --> 33:38.057
[exhales]

33:44.939 --> 33:45.815
Hey, ma'am?

33:49.235 --> 33:50.236
Ma'am?

33:50.319 --> 33:52.530
-Can you watch the box office for a bit?
-Mm-hmm.

33:57.618 --> 33:58.786
SHOWTIMES
GHOST

34:16.387 --> 34:17.388
[sighs]

34:20.224 --> 34:22.852
[gasps, moans excitedly]

34:22.935 --> 34:24.562
[giggles]

34:25.772 --> 34:28.149
-[moans excitedly]
-[kettle clatters]

34:29.609 --> 34:31.611
[grunts, kisses]

34:32.904 --> 34:36.157
It's really Christmas now.
The best Christmas ever.

34:36.240 --> 34:38.367
-That's why I'm here.
-[moans excitedly]

34:39.952 --> 34:42.288
Aw! Look at you in overalls, babe.

34:42.371 --> 34:44.082
Mm, you lost weight.

34:44.165 --> 34:45.708
You're so cute.

34:45.792 --> 34:46.834
[chuckles]

34:47.543 --> 34:49.545
[both moan, laugh]

34:57.929 --> 35:00.807
Should I flash the projector on them?
How do you know her?

35:02.266 --> 35:03.726
I don't really know her.

35:03.810 --> 35:05.645
[projectionist]
You helped a stranger get a job?

35:05.728 --> 35:08.856
Well… can't say I know her,

35:08.940 --> 35:10.691
but I can't say I don't either.

35:11.234 --> 35:12.985
Mm-hmm. So that's how it is.

35:13.694 --> 35:16.656
-Might be something between you one day.
-Nothing will happen.

35:17.156 --> 35:19.367
You never know between a man and a woman.

35:19.450 --> 35:22.829
Just because there's a goalie
doesn't mean you can't score.

35:22.912 --> 35:26.040
We wear hard hats on construction sites
because it's the safe thing to do.

35:26.124 --> 35:28.376
But secretly, you don't mind the danger.

35:28.459 --> 35:30.795
Nice story. You should make a movie.

35:31.838 --> 35:34.715
Why won't anything happen?
Are you related to her?

35:35.216 --> 35:36.050
No, It's just…

35:37.885 --> 35:40.555
We've seen each other
in very embarrassing situations.

35:45.309 --> 35:46.602
Why are they going back there?

35:47.395 --> 35:49.564
-You know exactly why.
-Sure.

35:51.524 --> 35:55.278
I don't want a girlfriend anymore, okay?
Especially not from ticket sales.

35:56.445 --> 35:59.282
Hey. Why are you talking to me
instead of her?

36:02.743 --> 36:04.537
God. This is crazy.

36:05.371 --> 36:08.207
[projectionist] Life is short,
and love is a rare privilege.

36:08.291 --> 36:10.418
[romantic pop music playing]

36:10.501 --> 36:11.377
[Yeong-beom] Here.

36:12.128 --> 36:14.046
-[Geum-myeong giggling]
-[chuckles]

36:16.132 --> 36:17.383
-You know what?
-What?

36:17.967 --> 36:20.136
-My family doesn't know.
-What?

36:20.636 --> 36:21.554
That I'm in Korea.

36:22.346 --> 36:24.390
I was supposed to come
at the end of the month,

36:24.932 --> 36:25.933
but I came early.

36:27.685 --> 36:29.478
You're a gangster, aren't you?

36:29.562 --> 36:30.771
Should I tell them?

36:32.523 --> 36:33.357
Should I?

36:35.443 --> 36:36.777
-You better not.
-[chuckles]

36:36.861 --> 36:39.906
You know, between you and a puppy,
you're the cuter one.

36:40.406 --> 36:41.532
[chuckles]

36:44.035 --> 36:45.870
[movie music playing]

36:45.953 --> 36:47.622
DAEHAN NEWS

36:55.379 --> 36:56.214
Hey, man.

36:57.173 --> 36:58.549
Why did you turn that on?

37:00.092 --> 37:02.386
[Geum-myeong] I got this place
because of the hilltop view.

37:03.679 --> 37:04.889
If we go all the way up,

37:04.972 --> 37:07.225
we'll see the biggest Christmas tree
in Korea.

37:07.308 --> 37:09.727
You won't see one that big
even in America.

37:11.354 --> 37:14.815
If I lived too close to the school,
friends would come over too often.

37:15.316 --> 37:17.735
Rooms near the school
are always in demand,

37:17.818 --> 37:19.779
so, of course,
all the landlords are jerks.

37:19.862 --> 37:21.030
PISS HERE, AND I'LL CUT IT OFF

37:21.113 --> 37:22.865
It's a relief these people don't feed me.

37:22.949 --> 37:24.325
Not that I eat much anyway.

37:24.408 --> 37:25.952
HELP US FIND OUR MISSING STUDENTS

37:27.161 --> 37:27.995
Geum-myeong.

37:28.788 --> 37:29.622
Huh?

37:30.414 --> 37:31.415
What is it?

37:33.042 --> 37:33.918
You can't live here.

37:34.543 --> 37:36.671
Look at this place.
It's worse than Harlem.

37:38.839 --> 37:40.758
The people who spray-paint that stuff,

37:41.300 --> 37:43.886
they gotta be sick in the head. Honestly.

37:44.720 --> 37:46.806
Why live in such a dangerous area?

37:47.598 --> 37:50.101
I can't sleep
knowing you live somewhere like this.

37:51.394 --> 37:54.021
Why are they fighting
in someone else's neighborhood?

38:02.446 --> 38:03.864
That man's an artist.

38:05.491 --> 38:07.201
He's the artist who works at our theater.

38:07.994 --> 38:09.078
Stop overreacting.

38:09.161 --> 38:12.039
[Yeong-beom] No one wants his girlfriend
to live in a place like this.

38:12.123 --> 38:13.249
I'm worried sick.

38:13.332 --> 38:17.086
What do you mean "place like this"?
I'm doing just fine here.

38:17.169 --> 38:18.087
[Yeong-beom sighs]

38:19.088 --> 38:20.381
Pack your things tonight.

38:22.091 --> 38:24.760
-Move to our neighborhood.
-[Geum-myeong] Where in your neighborhood?

38:25.344 --> 38:26.429
To your apartment?

38:26.512 --> 38:27.805
You really don't know Seoul.

38:27.888 --> 38:29.849
You're the one who doesn't know Seoul.

38:31.142 --> 38:32.059
Not me.

38:33.936 --> 38:34.854
[Yeong-beom sighs]

38:35.354 --> 38:38.232
I'm just saying this
because I'm worried about you.

38:40.151 --> 38:42.445
Just leave, okay?
I don't want you in my room.

38:42.528 --> 38:45.906
You're living in a Korean slum,
a place where serial murders happen.

38:45.990 --> 38:49.285
Then go back to America
if you're American now.

38:49.910 --> 38:50.745
I…

38:55.124 --> 38:56.375
You better not follow me.

38:57.209 --> 38:58.169
[scoffs]

39:04.091 --> 39:06.761
[man 2] The kid never smiles ever.
[scoffs]

39:07.428 --> 39:09.388
He keeps his mouth closed all the time.

39:09.472 --> 39:12.725
I couldn't even strike up
a conversation with him if I wanted to.

39:12.808 --> 39:15.561
Hey, can't you just eat from
the already open ones?

39:15.644 --> 39:17.772
Who do you think
he bought the dumplings for?

39:17.855 --> 39:19.273
So the kid could have some.

39:20.775 --> 39:23.819
Then stop yelling at him
and scaring him off.

39:23.903 --> 39:25.279
It's a waste of good money.

39:25.946 --> 39:27.323
Give them to him yourself.

39:28.032 --> 39:30.242
Our Picasso paints beautiful ladies

39:30.743 --> 39:32.745
without showing so much
as an inch of skin.

39:33.412 --> 39:35.122
Now, what sense does that make?

39:35.915 --> 39:37.917
[pensive music playing]

39:44.882 --> 39:48.969
AEMA WANTS TO RIDE AGAIN
MADAME AEMA

39:52.723 --> 39:55.726
Huh. How did he not get fired for this?

39:57.228 --> 39:58.187
[sighs]

40:26.465 --> 40:27.925
[music fades]

40:28.008 --> 40:29.677
Does he sleep here too?

40:34.473 --> 40:37.309
BAEK SEOK'S POETRY COLLECTION

40:39.728 --> 40:41.730
[distant siren wailing]

40:47.903 --> 40:50.614
ME, NATASHA, AND THE WHITE DONKEY

40:53.033 --> 40:55.369
THOUGH I'M POOR
I LOVED THE BEAUTIFUL NATASHA

40:55.453 --> 40:57.163
SO TONIGHT, THE SNOW WHUMPFS DOWN

40:58.956 --> 41:01.167
[Bu-seon] Because you're not
interested in money?

41:01.834 --> 41:04.795
Oh, I forgot!
You're a noble artist, aren't you?

41:06.380 --> 41:08.466
You're always saying
that I always talk about money,

41:08.549 --> 41:10.676
but, hey, I'm not the one who's poor.

41:10.759 --> 41:12.678
You feel noble
because you don't care about it,

41:12.761 --> 41:15.055
but every time we're together,
no matter what we do,

41:15.139 --> 41:17.391
I'm the one who has to worry about money
all the time.

41:17.475 --> 41:19.935
"How much was the pork cutlet?"
"How much is the movie ticket?"

41:20.019 --> 41:21.604
Whenever we plan a trip, I have to think,

41:21.687 --> 41:23.981
"Oh, he doesn't have money.
We can't do it."

41:24.064 --> 41:25.191
We dated for three years,

41:25.274 --> 41:27.276
and we've never been to
a Western restaurant.

41:27.359 --> 41:29.570
Always kalguksu,
jjolmyeon, kalguksu, jjolmyeon!

41:29.653 --> 41:32.406
[gasps] I swear I feel pathetic
being your girlfriend!

41:32.948 --> 41:34.742
Is that what art means?

41:34.825 --> 41:37.036
Tell me. Is that what art stands for?

41:37.620 --> 41:39.079
How much longer can this go on?

41:39.580 --> 41:43.042
How long until you've finished rebelling
and marry the man your father wants?

41:43.584 --> 41:46.879
Just leave. Don't worry about saving face.
Just get out of here.

41:46.962 --> 41:48.130
You're just letting me go?

41:48.214 --> 41:49.215
-I'm sick of this.
-What?

41:49.298 --> 41:51.759
While we've been together,
you went on six blind dates.

41:52.551 --> 41:53.761
I don't deserve this.

41:54.553 --> 41:55.387
I'm done.

41:56.222 --> 41:58.057
I've had enough of your disrespect.

42:00.017 --> 42:02.186
I don't even like you anymore. Just leave.

42:04.605 --> 42:05.648
Is there someone else?

42:07.525 --> 42:09.777
[phone ringing]

42:13.822 --> 42:15.032
There is a girl, isn't there?

42:16.116 --> 42:18.035
That's why you're pretending to be strong.

42:18.536 --> 42:19.578
Like you do?

42:19.662 --> 42:22.039
[phone ringing]

42:23.249 --> 42:24.583
Why won't you pick up the phone?

42:25.626 --> 42:28.629
You do have someone. I know.
And yet you pretended to be the victim.

42:28.712 --> 42:31.840
So what do you want me to do?
If I ask you to stay, will you?

42:32.841 --> 42:33.842
[scoffs]

42:36.971 --> 42:39.348
[Geum-myeong] I think
that was the exact moment

42:39.431 --> 42:40.891
when my landlord's daughter

42:40.975 --> 42:43.310
started kicking my shoes as she passed by.

42:43.394 --> 42:45.062
[jaunty music playing]

42:48.607 --> 42:51.777
Um, I brought you some dumplings.

42:52.945 --> 42:56.198
The projectionist asked me to do it.

42:57.199 --> 43:01.453
You know, I really don't know why
we end up in awkward situations.

43:02.580 --> 43:04.540
It gets worse every time, right?

43:05.165 --> 43:06.417
I don't believe this.

43:09.253 --> 43:11.547
PART-TIME USHER
CANNES THEATER

43:11.630 --> 43:13.090
Did you get her the job here?

43:15.134 --> 43:17.720
Wait. Uh… [sighs]

43:18.429 --> 43:20.806
So this is
your little secret at the theater.

43:21.599 --> 43:22.641
How sweet.

43:22.725 --> 43:24.184
Look, she even brought you food.

43:24.268 --> 43:25.561
Ah, uh…

43:25.644 --> 43:27.187
No, I--

43:27.271 --> 43:31.609
Hey, uh, little help? Maybe you could try
explaining to her what--

43:31.692 --> 43:33.110
I cannot believe this.

43:34.111 --> 43:35.362
You guys deserve each other.

43:36.196 --> 43:37.072
[Geum-myeong sighs]

43:38.032 --> 43:41.035
What a clueless girl.
She doesn't even know she's a third wheel.

43:41.785 --> 43:45.748
You're a high school dropout.
She goes to Seoul National University.

43:46.832 --> 43:47.666
Watch your mouth.

43:48.500 --> 43:49.835
[scoffs]

43:49.918 --> 43:52.755
[Geum-myeong] The fall breeze
turned into a spring wind.

43:53.339 --> 43:57.051
And the spring wind
continually howled in my heart.

43:57.134 --> 44:00.220
[kettle whistling]

44:00.304 --> 44:02.973
THE WIND GOES WHOOSH
MY HEART GOES BOO-HOO

44:03.057 --> 44:05.059
[funky pop music playing]

46:42.299 --> 46:43.592
[music ends]

46:48.722 --> 46:53.477
"JUST GET READY AND GO,
RIDE THE MOMENT WITH ALL YOU HAVE."
